This just shifts the complaint one step further away; vikeys users will
now complain whenever they hit someone to their northwest ('y').

I've toyed with making conducts hard-enforced (ie. you don't have a
choice to #pray, even if you want to), but it only works for some of
them, and has to be tweaked a bit for things like "weaponless" where one
of the useful tools (pickaxe) serves as both a tool and a weapon.

There's also the other side of the coin where this _is_ a turn-based
game, and as such being overprompty is removing one of the valid
measures of skill in the game -- ie., learning how to not bang on the
keyboard like a hypercaffeinated monkey on meth.  (Yes, I am aware this
isn't what solidsnail was doing.)

